PHASE 1 — ORIENT (Dependency & Sequencing Analysis)
================================================================================

## 1.1 Dependency Graph

```
ProductsFilterSortDrawersWrapper
├── Prop: categoryPath → catalogueKeys (rename)
├── Calls: getFiltersForCategoryPath(catalogueKeys)
├── Calls: getSortablesForCategoryPath(catalogueKeys)
└── Used by:
    ├── [...category]/page.tsx
    └── products/page.tsx

Filter/Sort Functions
├── Accept: catalogueKeys: string[]
├── Internally: Query by VFS keys ✓
├── Then: Read category field (indirection)
└── Then: Query filters by category name (indirection)
    └── Target: Direct VFS key → filter mapping

Search
├── Independent of filter/sort
├── Can integrate with VFS keys as optional enhancement
└── No dependencies on other gaps
```

## 1.2 Sequencing Rationale

**Order Determination**:
1. **Regression Tests First** — Must validate current behavior before changes
2. **Prop Rename (Gap A)** — Foundation for all other component work
3. **Filter/Sort Optimization (Gap D)** — Builds on proper prop naming
4. **Dead Code Removal (Gap B, C)** — Safe after verifying not used
5. **Search Integration (Gap E)** — Independent, can be deferred

## 1.3 Sprint Boundaries

**In Scope**:
- Professional prop naming alignment
- Query optimization (eliminate category indirection)
- Dead code identification and removal
- Regression test suite for affected areas

**Out of Scope**:
- Schema changes to Sanity (assumes existing structure)
- New UI components for search filters
- Performance benchmarking
- Full test coverage of unrelated areas

**Forbidden**:
- Breaking changes to product page URLs
- Changes to filter/sort UI appearance
- Modifications to VFS build script (already fixed)
- Any change affecting checkout flow

